  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::483",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin appears to interact with Atp1b3 through a shared pathway involving the sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Acetyldigitoxin binds to Fxyd2, which participates in both potassium-transporting and sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase activities. These activities are ultimately linked to Atp1b3, indicating a potential role for Acetyldigitoxin in modulating Atp1b3 function. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent interaction, though the specific mechanism of how Acetyldigitoxin influences Atp1b3 remains partially obscured. The overlapping participation of Fxyd2 in different ATPase activities implies that Acetyldigitoxin may regulate Atp1b3 through a common intermediary, possibly by altering the activity or expression of Fxyd2. This integrated pathway highlights the importance of Fxyd2 in linking Acetyldigitoxin to Atp1b3, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
